// Rule: [T1003.004] Papercut Agentic Campaign - Registry Hive Staging
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1003.004
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Hunts source-observed reg.exe and certutil.exe staging commands for SYSTEM/ SECURITY hives using the campaign's pc-* filenames.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for registry hive staging using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: successful exploitation, malicious ownership, downstream impact, campaign attribution or complete compromise without corroborating evidence.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// PaperCut campaign - SYSTEM/SECURITY hive staging with reg.exe or certutil.exe
// Status: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint / DeviceProcessEvents
// Logic type: Campaign-specific artifact
// Exact paths and filenames were published by GreyNoise and are mutable.
// No result proves exfiltration, DCSync, credential recovery, or PaperCut exploitation.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where
    (
        FileName =~ "reg.exe"
        and ProcessCommandLine has "save"
        and (
            ProcessCommandLine contains @"HKLM\SYSTEM"
            or ProcessCommandLine contains @"HKLM\SECURITY"
        )
        and ProcessCommandLine has_any (
            "pc-sys.hiv",
            "pc-sec.hiv",
            "pc-security.hiv",
            "pc-system.hiv",
            "pc-sys-reg.hiv"
        )
    )
    or
    (
        FileName =~ "certutil.exe"
        and ProcessCommandLine contains "-encode"
        and ProcessCommandLine has_any (
            "pc-sys.hiv",
            "pc-sec.hiv",
            "pc-security.hiv",
            "pc-system.hiv",
            "pc-sys-reg.hiv"
        )
        and ProcessCommandLine contains ".b64"
    )
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    AccountDomain,
    AccountName,
    FileName,
    FolderPath,
    ProcessCommandLine,
    ProcessId,
    ProcessUniqueId,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
